WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.888 --> 00:00:08.928
On the wedding morning, wedding-parent makeup happens on a pre-set schedule.

2
00:00:09.264 --> 00:00:16.680
Most shops book appointments minute by minute, and on the day, the focus has to be on the makeup and hair itself, leaving no time for a detailed consultation.

3
00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:20.856
Everything has to finish on time so you can head straight to the wedding hall.

4
00:00:21.192 --> 00:00:25.896
"How would you like it done?" they ask, then go straight into makeup and hair styling.

5
00:00:26.232 --> 00:00:31.128
It's better to spend the limited time on the makeup itself rather than on consultation.

6
00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:40.392
If you're meeting for the first time that morning and only then start thinking about the style, you may end up heading to the venue with a look you don't like and no time to fix it.

7
00:00:40.728 --> 00:00:49.752
In short, it's hard to reflect each parent's specific needs on the day, and it's too risky to leave the quality of photos that will last a lifetime up to chance.

8
00:00:50.088 --> 00:00:55.176
The wedding day itself should be a time to perfectly execute a style you've already prepared, not a time for consultation.

9
00:00:55.512 --> 00:00:58.248
"They'll just figure it out" is not a safe bet.
